    {
      "evidence_id": "E-QCOMEM-60-OPPOINT-20260903A",
      "status": "verified_fresh_source_frozen_terminal_complete",
      "purpose": "Operating-point gate registered in advance as action A16: supply the quantized exact-cache baseline the round-44 panel required, and decide whether the split depth moves from 7 to 13 under a preregistered rule that adopts 13 only if it holds full-prefix quality on the full 60-item cohort. It does not, so j=7 stands. The run also supplies the 60-item TTFT and TPOT figures and an independent replication of the archival paired difference.",
      "artifact_paths": [
        "runs/qcomem/r45-d7d13-60item-20260903a/length-sweep-shard-{0..7}.json",
        "runs/qcomem/r45-d7d13-60item-20260903a/rank-{0..7}.log"
      ],
      "replay_boundary": "Executions: QS Job 264196 Trial 1943447 produced seven of eight ranks; rank 6 stopped at the runner's dense_semantics_gate and contributed no rows, so that trial alone is an incomplete execution and is not evidence on its own. QS Job 264381 Trial 1943737 staged a fix to that gate and re-ran rank 6 alone into the same run directory, completing the cohort at 900 rows = 5 configurations x 60 items x 3 repeats, all eight shards status completed. Extraction is QS Job 264398 Trial 1943780. The gate fix is recorded because it changes what the gate asserts: run_dense_semantics_gate had computed first-token agreement across all three traces including the two-chunk full-prefix arm, while its own semantic string requires agreement only between the two single-chunk dense arms and states that cross-chunk-boundary equality is diagnostic. Rank 6 carried an item on which those paths diverge, which archived 60-item evidence measures at 6 of 60 items. The assertion now covers the two dense arms and full-prefix agreement is retained as the diagnostic field first_token_agrees_with_full_prefix, which reported False for rank 6 while dense agreement reported True. The pre-fix module is preserved on the cluster as qcomem_deployment_arms.py.bak_pre_gatefix. Protocol: 60-item Qasper/2WikiMQA validation cohort, source indices 6--35, real LongBench protocol with --eos-policy stop and --generation-limit-policy dataset, 4096-token input cap, one warm-up, three repeats, seed 20260903, group size 64, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-59d61f3, torch 2.11.0+cu129, transformers 5.14.1, one H20-3e per rank. Statistics: item F1 averaged over repeats, then paired differences against full-prefix-q16 over the 60 common item keys with 10,000 item-level bootstrap resamples at seed 20260903 and percentile intervals. Boundary: no paired interval exists between frozen depth-7 and full-prefix Q8; the 5.84x retained-state ratio between them is bit-width confounded and decomposes as 3.9174x split times 1.4912x width; per-request transient working set is not measured by this run."
